    "body": "<h1>Quickstart</h1>
<p>The fastest path from zero to a running <a href="{{cms:item/1c05e59d-f366-4176-a6ca-8f52ccfb3ce6}}">pipeline</a>.</p>

<h2>1. Get an API key</h2>
<p>See <a href="{{cms:item/67e28ef9-df46-446a-9839-8f4bd0b23de1}}">Authentication</a> if you don't have one yet.</p>

<h2>2. Create a pipeline</h2>

<h3>Bash</h3>
{{ds:component/code-block|filename=terminal|language=bash|code=curl -X POST https://api.godzilladocs.dev/v2/pipelines \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $GODZILLA_API_KEY" \\
  -d '{\"name\":\"my-first-pipeline\",\"source_connector_id\":\"conn_demo_source\",\"destination_connector_id\":\"conn_demo_dest\"}'}}

<h3>Go</h3>
{{ds:component/code-block|filename=main.go|language=go|code=package main

import (
	"context"
	"log"
	"os"

	"github.com/godzilla-io/godzilla-go/client"
)

func main() {
	apiKey := os.Getenv("GODZILLA_API_KEY")
	c := client.New(apiKey)

	pipeline, err := c.Pipelines.Create(context.Background(), &client.CreatePipelineRequest{
		Name:                   "my-first-pipeline",
		SourceConnectorID:      "conn_demo_source",
		DestinationConnectorID: "conn_demo_dest",
	})
	if err != nil {
		log.Fatalf("failed to create pipeline: %v", err)
	}

	log.Printf("created pipeline: %s", pipeline.ID)
}}}

<h2>3. Watch it run</h2>
<p>Subscribe to <code>pipeline.completed</code> via <a href="{{cms:item/bb137086-ba77-4d11-87e6-36de66c72b7d}}">Webhooks</a>, or poll the <a href="{{cms:item/25d4407d-805e-4f94-98d3-652ae78978d4}}">Events endpoint</a> to see events as they're processed.</p>

{{ds:component/alert|variant=success|title=That's it|body_html=<p>For a fuller walkthrough with a real source and destination, go to <a href="{{cms:item/2df76640-838b-4256-956e-d8a19a602241}}">Building your first pipeline</a> in the Guides section.</p>}}

